## The exploitation models

The label is a KEV listing within 180 days of publication, and the population starts on
the day KEV could first list a CVE within that window (DECISIONS.md, the change request on the
exploitation population). The floor is a logistic regression with balanced class weights; LightGBM
reads the same day 0 features and the band floor's four probabilities, taken out of fold for the
CVEs the band floor was fit on and from the committed floor, the one the API serves, for the rest. Its search, {{ plan.models.exploit_lgbm.search }}, runs on the half
year folds of that change request.

{% if has("models.rank.lgbm.dev_average_precision") %}
On development, LightGBM's average precision is {{ v("models.rank.lgbm.dev_average_precision") }}
against the floor's {{ v("models.rank.floor.dev_average_precision") }}, and it holds
{{ v("models.rank.lgbm.dev_recall_at_top5") }} of the development listings in its top
five percent, against {{ v("models.rank.floor.dev_recall_at_top5") }} for the floor.
{% if raw("models.rank.lgbm.dev_average_precision") < raw("models.rank.floor.dev_average_precision") and raw("models.rank.lgbm.dev_recall_at_top5") > raw("models.rank.floor.dev_recall_at_top5") %}
So LightGBM is behind the floor at the very top of its ranking, where average precision weighs most,
and ahead across the top five percent, the depth C2 judges. Both are reported, and C2 is judged on
LightGBM, the exploitation model the operating points name.
{% endif %}
{% if raw("models.rank.lgbm.dev_average_precision") < raw("models.rank.floor.dev_average_precision") and raw("models.rank.lgbm.dev_recall_at_top5") < raw("models.rank.floor.dev_recall_at_top5") %}
LightGBM is behind its floor on both measures in this run.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if has("models.rank.runs") %}
The exploitation step has been run {{ v("models.rank.runs.count") }} times on the same rows, and its
search chose different trees each time: over the runs, LightGBM's development recall in the top five
percent ranges from {{ v("models.rank.runs.lgbm_recall_low") }} to {{ v("models.rank.runs.lgbm_recall_high") }}, while the floor's stays between
{{ v("models.rank.runs.floor_recall_low") }} and {{ v("models.rank.runs.floor_recall_high") }}. The first run projected with its own refit of the band floor and was
replaced by a run on the committed floor (DECISIONS.md, the exploitation run reads the committed band
floor). That run, repeated on another runner, chose other trees again: the processor and its BLAS
threads move the band floor's out of fold sums in their last bits, and fifty trials over three folds
with few listings each turn those bits into different trees (DECISIONS.md, the exploitation rerun,
and the exploitation step pins its numeric kernels).
{% if raw("models.rank.runs.model_pinned") == "yes" %}
The model is the run with the numeric kernels pinned. Refit on the build machine, another processor,
with the same pins, it gave the same number for every value of its record's manifest part and every
score of every CVE (results/models/rank_reproduction.json), the first run of this step to reproduce,
so it replaced the rerun under the rule committed before it ran. Its trees are still one draw of an
unstable search, and test judges them.
{% else %}
The rerun stands: the run with the numeric kernels pinned did not give the same numbers when refit on
the build machine, so the rule committed before it ran kept the rerun.
{% endif %}

